# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2026-08-12 PROVENANCE FIX. These four are IMPORTED AT RUNTIME by main.py and are
# baked into the image by COPY . ., yet the rules above hid them from git. Their
# source existed only on Bifrost's disk and inside built images, so a clean-clone
# build shipped without them -- that is the v303 crash of 2026-08-03, and it is why
# build.ps1 is mandatory and git archive is banned.
#
# igor_prompt.py is additionally on the PROTECTED list in protected_files.json
# (rule 1, 'agent operating instructions = policy config-of-record'), so the
# protected-file ceremony was running pre/post SHA against a file git did not track,
# with no history to diff and no way to recover a prior revision.
#
# Negations, not deletions: ag_*.py above still legitimately hides scratch
# (rag_query*.py, rag_recheck.py, rag_collections_probe.py). Only the imported one
# is exempted. Check main.py's import list before adding to this block.
!igor_prompt.py
!overlay_dispatch.py
!npu_classifier_shadow.py
!rag_inject_chromadb.py

# 2026-10-05: ceremony preimages accumulate here (32 files, 3.6 MB). .dockerignore
# already excludes backups/ AND *-preimage-*, so they never reach the image -- but
# untracked they keep `git status` dirty, and build.ps1 aborts on a dirty tree.
backups/
